From: Shagg <shagg.dev88@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] patch104 (GitHub #245): Xbox One / Series impulse triggers - InputSystem::SetTriggerRumble (--pad_trigger_rumble, off by default)

SDL_RumbleGamepadTriggers on the SDL pads of one player that report SDL_PROP_GAMEPAD_CAP_TRIGGER_RUMBLE_BOOLEAN (others:
no write); strengths 0-65535 and a duration SDL times (1 ms - 1 s; 0, 0 = stop). Nothing is sent - and a running pulse
is stopped - while --vibration is off, while COGBox's UI blocks input, or while the game's window is not in front.
On Windows the cvar also sets SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_RAWINPUT before the gamepad subsystem starts: SDL 3.4's default Xbox
path is XInput, which has no trigger motors; its raw input driver drives them through Windows.Gaming.Input (SDL
disabled it by default in May 2025 because Windows could stop delivering raw controller input until a reboot - hence
off by default). With it on, every XInput-class pad (Xbox 360, X-mode pads, Steam Input's virtual pad) is read by
raw input: other SDL GUIDs, a combined trigger axis, no Guide and no rumble until the pad's first input pairs it with
XInput / WGI (a failed rumble is sent again with that input), and pads in raw input's order (split screen may differ
from the ring lights). Over Bluetooth Windows may drive no trigger motors even where SDL reports them.
One log line per pad says whether its trigger motors are reachable (with SDL's path: "XInput#n" = the XInput
driver), one when the first pulse lands, one (per pad) when a pulse fails.
New exports: InputSystem::SetTriggerRumble, InputSystem::TriggerRumbleEnabled - ship the runtime with the exe.
New members are appended after patch 98's (InputSystem, SDLInputDriver); InputDriver's vtable is unchanged.

